{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\nss=['s-read-contract','s-read-mode','s-read-memory-test','s-read-entry','s-read-context','s-transfer-read','s-read-result','s-follower','s-api','s-ready-storage','s-storage-writes']\nsub=dict(action='review',artifact_id='67a08845713a4e00bec3fa0cfa58c569',rationale='Review the completed read-context check as a whole against its v1 requirement and binding, retaining its request-correlation scope.',review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=ss,rationale='Fixed artifact 67a08845713a4e00bec3fa0cfa58c569 checks claim-read-context-correlation v1 through binding-read-context v1. The request-specific Node contract and safe-mode quorum communication apply to distinct nonempty contexts in this static non-singleton cluster; same-context retries, singleton and lease modes are excluded. The actual driver creates a shared compacted prefix with public MemoryStorage APIs, campaigns node 1, and completes actual election/no-op Ready work before reading. It runs the old request to completion and retains an actual follower-produced heartbeat response from the same execution. It then invokes the fresh context, accepts but does not deliver its heartbeat, replays the unmodified old response through RawNode.Step, and records actual Ready.ReadStates. Local persistence and application work follow the async FIFO contract; no critical target state is assigned. Missing ticks during this finite interval do not create an authority proof or affect the selected context lookup. The old_completed -> admitted -> stale_processed prerequisites have explicit alias references; identity is the operation, endpoints, unchanged term and fresh context, independent of compared read counts. The replay endpoint is Step completion and draining available leader Ready, not a timeout. The eventual completed event additionally requires an actual fresh response and fresh ReadState in this same run, so a permitted pending state is never called a liveness violation. Run f77d391be79c41b7a6f289f68917051d records old_read_count=1, distinct contexts=true, replayed_term=2, fresh_replies_before=0 and fresh_read_count=0. The completed result preserves prequorum_fresh_reads=0 and reports fresh_replies_after=1, final_fresh_reads=1, read_index=2 and final_term=2. Thus the one-way necessity comparison is exercised, and the genuine response control completes regardless of the earlier observation. Source recvAck ignores an absent old context and advance previously removed that context, explaining the bounded result. No open correspondence issue was found for these fixed inputs.',counterevidence=[],limitations=['One old-response replay and one fresh invocation in a two-voter static configuration; not a general linearizability proof.','ReadState release is the library endpoint. No client return or actual state-machine value is observed.','The test does not distinguish every possible internal reason for withholding output; source context lookup explains the observed protection.','Same-context retry legality, retained pre-commit reads across terms, lease mode and configuration changes remain independent questions.','MemoryStorage and a no-op application implement caller duties without measuring physical disk durability.'])],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['67a08845713a4e00bec3fa0cfa58c569','f77d391be79c41b7a6f289f68917051d','s-read-context','s-read-contract','s-role','s-read-release'],answered='Actual old-context support did not release the distinct fresh read before its genuine quorum response. The fresh request then completed in the same term/history. This supports bounded request-context isolation and does not infer a client-level linearizability result.',remaining=['The version-qualified same-context retry permission remains unresolved in this source snapshot.','The retained pre-commit request queue and configuration-dependent quorum changes are not covered by this execution.','The synchronous persistence-ordering documentation conflict remains independently retained.'],understanding='unchanged',rationale='Both selected executable units now have completed comparisons and this review supplies the missing correspondence for the second. Next compare the retained frontier and clarify whether the pending pre-commit read path adds an applicable responsibility beyond the API permission to lose requests, before proposing more execution.',question_updates={'26f8ae78af1542f2a6ca3df474407836':dict(unknowns=['Unmeasured term/configuration transitions and same-context retries are outside the completed distinct-context replay scope.'],resume_conditions=[])}))\nPath('submission.json').write_text(json.dumps(sub,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));x=subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True);print(x.stdout);print(x.stderr)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
